# wted-org Project Rules

## Project Overview
wted-org is a Next.js static export project serving as the unified platform for WTED Goose Radio,
the WTED community (Discourse forum integration), and the Dripfield.pro setlist archive.
It is deployed on Netlify as a fully static site with zero serverless function invocations at runtime.
All server-side logic lives in Supabase Edge Functions.

---

## Architecture Rules

### Static Export — Non-Negotiable
- This project uses `output: "export"` in next.config.ts. Never remove or disable this.
- Never suggest or introduce server-side Next.js features including:
  - API routes (`app/api/` or `pages/api/`)
  - Server components using `getServerSideProps` or `getInitialProps`
  - The `"use server"` directive
  - Next.js middleware (`middleware.ts` or `middleware.js`)
  - Intercepting routes (e.g. `@modal/(.)route/page.tsx`)
- If a problem seems to require one of the above, the correct solution is a Supabase Edge Function,
  not a Next.js server feature.

### Supabase Edge Functions — Server-Side Home
- All server-side logic (API proxying, auth token validation, rate limiting, external HTTP calls,
  service role key usage) must live in Supabase Edge Functions under `/supabase/functions/`.
- Follow the existing Edge Function patterns in this project:
  - Include proper CORS headers (use `_shared/cors.ts`)
  - Use the Supabase client initialized with the service role key from environment variables
  - Include proper error handling and status codes
- Client-side code calls Edge Functions via the Supabase Edge Function URL pattern:
  `${SUPABASE_URL}/functions/v1/function-name`
- Never add a new API route to solve a problem that an Edge Function can handle.

### Client-Side Data Fetching
- All Supabase database queries are made client-side using the Supabase JS client
  with the anon key (`NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`).
- Never move client-side Supabase queries to a server component or API route.
- Follow existing pagination patterns using `.range()` in 1000-record batches
  to avoid Supabase's default row limit.

---

## Routing Rules

### Dynamic Routes — Always Need generateStaticParams
- Every dynamic route segment (`[id]`, `[show_id]`, etc.) must have a `generateStaticParams`
  function that fetches all valid IDs from Supabase at build time.
- `generateStaticParams` uses `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL` and `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`
  which are available at build time.
- Never create a new dynamic route without also implementing `generateStaticParams`.

### User-Specific Pages — Query Params Only
- Pages that depend on a user ID that is not known at build time must use query params,
  not dynamic route segments.
- Pattern: `/archive/user?tab=overview&id=xxx` (and other `tab` slugs from `PROFILE_STATS_TABS`). Legacy `/archive/user/{tab}?id=` **301** to `?tab=` + `&id=` via `public/_redirects`.
- Use `lib/user-profile-url.ts` (`getUserProfileUrl`) for generating user profile URLs consistently.
- Never create a dynamic route segment for user IDs or any other runtime-only identifier.

### Modals
- Modals must be implemented as client-side components triggered by query params
  (e.g. `?submit=1`), not as intercepting routes.
- See `components/submit-modal-handler.tsx` and `app/(main)/layout.tsx` as the reference pattern.

---

## Image Rules

### Remote Images Always Need unoptimized
- Every `next/image` (`<Image>`) component that uses a remote `src` must include the
  `unoptimized` prop.
- The Next.js Image Optimization API is not available in static export mode.
- When adding a new `<Image>` with a remote src, always include `unoptimized`.

---

## Environment Variables

### Build-Time Variables
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL` and `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` must be set in the
  Netlify build environment. These are used by `generateStaticParams` functions and
  redirect pages at build time.
- Never use server-only (non-`NEXT_PUBLIC_`) environment variables in page components
  or layouts. They will not be available at runtime in a static export.
- Secrets (service role keys, Radio.co API keys, Discourse API keys) belong exclusively
  in Supabase Edge Function environment variables, never in the Next.js app.

---

## General Development Rules

- Always run `next build` to verify the static export succeeds before considering any
  feature complete.
- Do not modify existing Supabase Edge Functions, RLS policies, or database schema
  unless explicitly asked.
- Do not modify `lib/supabase.ts` (the Supabase client config) unless explicitly asked.
- When in doubt about where logic belongs — client component vs Edge Function — default
  to client component with a direct Supabase query. Only use an Edge Function when
  server-side execution is genuinely required (secrets, external API proxying, rate limiting).
